            "type": "text",
            "title": "Hello, Terminal! 👋",
            "content": "## Opening the Terminal\n\n- **Linux**: `Ctrl + Alt + T` or search 'Terminal'\n- **macOS**: Spotlight → 'Terminal'\n- **Windows (WSL)**: Install WSL, then open Ubuntu.\n\nYou'll see a prompt like `user@machine:~$ `. That's Bash waiting for your orders!"
        },
        {
            "id": "s_l2_2",
            "type": "code",
            "title": "Say Something with echo 🗣️",
            "content": "`echo` prints text to the screen. Simple but essential.\n\nTry it:",
            "codeSnippet": "echo \"Hello, Cybron!\"",
            "codeLanguage": "bash_scripting",
            "canRunCode": true
        },
